cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite this software and the relevant
  Dynamic Sensorium or Mental-Pong papers and datasets listed in the README
  and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
title: "Evaluating Dynamic Neural Encoding Beyond Response Correlation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Xiaotian
    email: xiaotian_zhu@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2956-8476"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/124585083/neural-trajectory-evaluation"
url: "https://github.com/124585083/neural-trajectory-evaluation"
abstract: >-
  A controlled comparison of Static and total-parameter-matched Dynamic neural
  encoding models using response accuracy, output-space RSA/CKA, and a frozen
  neural-data-defined GPFA trajectory assay on Dynamic Sensorium 2023.
  A separate Mental-Pong study compares objective and behavior-constrained
  position targets using condition-mean neural representations and linear
  readouts, with cross-scoring and randomization controls.
keywords:
  - neural encoding
  - Dynamic Sensorium
  - GPFA
  - neural population trajectories
  - representational similarity analysis
  - centered kernel alignment
  - Mental-Pong
  - condition-mean neural response
